      "side": 1,
      "message": "It should be possible to use the same trick I use for HChaCha: make a very thin wrapper function that only allocates the *Cipher, and let that be mid-stack inlined. I\u0027ll try it. What\u0027s the best benchmark to look at? arm64 ChaCha20-Poly1305?\n\nI have to say that I am pretty tired of fighting the inliner to this extent, though. In any case I am not going to introduce endianness concerns in a public API for performance reasons, as much as I do want to see the individual components be fast enough to replace the combined assembly.\n\nAnyway, yeah Uint32 should be an intrinsic, I thought it already was.",
